{
 "_note": "Sound (design 05 §7; 14 §7 T6). A recipe is a list of layers: w (square, sine, triangle, saw, noise), f [from, to] Hz (a sweep) or notes [Hz, ...] (one after another over ms), ms, env (fast, decay, tail, flat), band (noise: a band-pass centre in Hz; low / high: lowpass 300 / highpass 4000), q, gain, delay (ms), vib (vibrato Hz), trem (tremolo Hz), rep (repeats, gap ms). loud: Quiet surprises softens it. Volumes 0 to 1.",
 "volume": { "sfx": 0.7, "music": 0.4 },
 "mix": { "_note": "05 §7: at most maxVoices at once; the same sound again within dedupeMs is dropped; with more than crowdFrom creatures on screen the sound scales down by crowdFrom / count. Scale-aware (14 §2): zoomed right out a sound plays at farGain; a sound further than margin px off the screen is not heard. Quiet surprises: a loud recipe plays at quietGain.", "maxVoices": 8, "dedupeMs": 60, "crowdFrom": 200, "farGain": 0.35, "quietGain": 0.3, "margin": 64, "master": 0.5 },
