 "music": {
  "_note": "05 §7: four loops, 16 bars, pentatonic so they overlap without clashing; square lead, triangle bass, noise hat; night drops the lead an octave and removes the hat; danger cross-fades in with dangerFoes hostiles on screen, out after dangerCalmSec of calm. files: Stephen's tracks by name (a URL next to the game; empty: the synth plays); a slot may be a LIST, played in turn (23 Sep: his eight songs, free, by mood: the day's five, the night's two, danger's one; the sea and the snow keep the synth). night: after dark with nothing dangerous in view, when it has songs; its synth loop is the meadow's, so a song that fails to load sounds as a night always did. The songs live on the arcade at /music/v1/tiny-world/ (the private lucid-winds-music repo), never in git. root: a MIDI note.",
  "files": { "meadow": "", "night": "", "danger": "", "sea": "", "cold": "" },
  "_songs": "23 Sep 2026, Stephen: the radio is a MUSIC PLAYER (src/audio/songs.js). Three songs to start, the rest unlocked by minutes of play (the game unpaused), every song played WHOLE, one after another, each with a switch in the menu. No song is picked by what is on screen any more: that is what cut every song off after five seconds to a minute (a pan across water, a foe on screen, nightfall). The synth loops above stay ONLY as the offline fallback. Titles are his files' names made readable: his to correct.",
